        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs: clarify requestStart behavior for canceled requests in Performance API]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41704</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41704"/>
        <updated>2025-10-27T14:30:02.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56753804?u=0f698c1d89d7bc8d64ee9c423a5549147a91b866&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarifies in the Performance API documentation that canceled HTTP requests are still recorded as performance entries, but their <code class="notranslate">requestStart</code> timestamp will be 0. This update helps developers avoid calculation errors when analyzing performance metrics for canceled requests.</p>]]></content>
